From 3391449514ad7f9b1e9d527195b656b5e3afc859 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cortex Security Patch <cortex-agent@local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 22:34:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(security): notion/github-style glow cards + merged
 per-group insight cards

Phase Sec-4 -- follow-up to the previous security-agent-visibility
commit, addressing UI feedback on it directly.

- globals.css: new .tile-card / .tile-icon component classes -- a
  16px-radius card plus a small colored icon glow (radial background +
  soft box-shadow halo via --tile-color), restrained the same way every
  other glow effect in this file already is (a wash + a hairline ring,
  not a neon card). This is the 'big card with a small glow' language
  the /security pages now use throughout, in place of the previous plain
  tables.
- /security: 'Per-host posture' is now a grid of big host cards (icon
  glow tinted by aggregate status, host/role, a 2x2 grid of the four
  sub-check pills) instead of a table row per host. The category
  browse tiles below it now use the same tile-card/tile-icon treatment.
- /security/security-groups: same big-card treatment per host, each card
  showing its status pill, every currently-attached group as a chip
  (flagged red when it's the specific one carrying a signal), and a
  risky-rules/drift-count summary row.
- /security/security-groups/{hostname}: the three previously-separate
  sections (current groups / overly-permissive rules / drift) are now
  one detailed card per security group -- every rule the group actually
  holds, each tagged inline 'Risky' (with its specific reason) and/or
  'Added' if it's new since the last snapshot, plus any rule the last
  snapshot had that's gone now, shown struck through as 'Removed'. This
  replaces the old 'three counts, cross-reference them yourself' view
  with one place that shows exactly what a group contains and why it's
  flagged.
- lib/securityStatus.ts: new buildGroupInsights() -- matches a rule
  across data.security_groups/risky_rules/drift by its
  (direction, protocol, ports, remote_cidr) identity, since none of the
  three carry a shared rule id, and folds them into one annotated list
  per group (plus overallSecurityTone() for the new host cards' single
  aggregate color).

Verified with tsc --noEmit, eslint, and a full 'next build' (all
/security* routes compile and prerender/build cleanly).
